<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="..\config8\suzuki.xsl" ?>
<!DOCTYPE suzuki [
<!ENTITY % sdatacharaents SYSTEM "..\config8\sdatacharaents.txt">
%sdatacharaents;
]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "1E">
<servcat sctnbr = "01" scnbr = "05">
<configtype typenbr = "2">
<servinfotype sitcode = "4">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1524001" svcinfotypenbr = "06" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Oil Pressure Check
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Before checking oil pressure, check the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil level in oil pan
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If oil level is low, add oil up to FULL level mark (hole) (1) on oil level gauge. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1526001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<figure page = "2">
<graphic graphicname = "IYSQ01020012.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "45.200mm" ver = "01" gw = "160" gh = "111"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
2.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
LOW level mark (hole)
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil quality
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If oil is discolored or deteriorated, change it. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1526001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil leakage
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If leakage is found, repair leaky point.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Place gear shift lever in “Neutral”, apply parking brake and block drive wheels.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Start engine and warm up it to normal operating temperature.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Stop engine and turn off all electric switches.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
With ignition “OFF”, connect SUZUKI scan tool to DLC (1).
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1E208">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "NNNNN-00035">
SUZUKI scan tool (Suzuki SDT-II)
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A131015.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "87.737mm" ver = "01" gw = "205" gh = "232"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check “Oil Pump Absolute Pressure” under “Data List” mode on scan tool under the following condition.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Measure oil pressure at 4,000 rpm respectively
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Oil pressure specification
</title>
<ptxt>
130 to 230 kPa (1.3 to 2.3 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 18.8 to 33.3 psi, 1.3 to 2.3 bar)
</ptxt>
</spec>
</item>
</list1>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Stop engine.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
After completing the check, set ignition “OFF” and disconnect SUZUKI scan tool from DLC.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfo>
</servinfotype>
</configtype>
</servcat>
</section></manual></suzuki>
